>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_cond_depth`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_cond_depth : int -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sets the side-condition depth limit of a simpset.

With `set_cond_depth n ss`, a conditional rewrite is not applied if its
conditions would make the stack of side conditions being proved longer
than `n`. A simpset without this setting uses the value of
`Cond_rewr.stack_limit` (initially 4) when it is used.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val decide = {name = "decide", solve = K DECIDE} : Traverse.ssolver;
>>_ val ss = simpLib.add_unsafe_solver decide bool_ss;
>>+ SIMP_CONV (simpLib.set_cond_depth 0 ss)
      [arithmeticTheory.LESS_MOD] “x MOD (x + 1)”;
>> SIMP_CONV (simpLib.set_cond_depth 1 ss)
     [arithmeticTheory.LESS_MOD] “x MOD (x + 1)”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.set_subgoaler`](#simpLib.set_subgoaler),
[`simpLib.set_term_ord`](#simpLib.set_term_ord).
